# OTP Authentication System

This project has been updated to use One-Time Password (OTP) authentication instead of magic links. Here's how the new system works:

## Key Changes

1. **6-digit OTP codes** instead of magic link tokens
2. **15-minute expiry** for all OTP codes
3. **Signed JWT tokens** for OTP verification security
4. **Copy button** in email templates for easy OTP copying
5. **Development logging** for easy debugging during development

## API Endpoints

### 1. User Registration

```
POST /api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "role": "user"
}
```

**Response:**

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "User registered successfully. Please check your email for the verification code.",
  "data": {
    "user": { ... },
    "verificationToken": "signed-jwt-token"
  }
}
```

### 2. Login (Request OTP)

```
POST /api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}
```

**Response:**

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Login code sent to your email address.",
  "data": {
    "loginToken": "signed-jwt-token"
  }
}
```

### 3. Verify OTP (Email Verification or Login)

```
POST /api/v1/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "otp": "123456",
  "token": "signed-jwt-token-from-previous-step"
}
```

**Response:**

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Email verified successfully! Welcome to Task Flow.",
  "data": {
    "user": { ... },
    "accessToken": "jwt-access-token"
  }
}
```

### 4. Resend Verification OTP

```
POST /api/v1/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}
```

### 5. Request Login OTP (Alternative to login endpoint)

```
POST /api/v1/auth/request-login-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}
```

